<!-- These are *vocabulary* lists, not positional arrays: each language names as many words as
     it needs, and they are unioned across languages at runtime. InconsistentArrays compares
     item counts between locales, which is meaningless here.

     Chinese has no word spaces and no plural inflection. Substring matching has no word
     boundary, so every aisle and protein keyword is at least two characters — a lone 油 would
     fire on 油菜/油条/牛油果, a lone 鸡 on 鸡蛋, a lone 牛 on 牛奶/牛油果 and a lone 羊 on 羊奶.
     Units, by contrast, are prefix-matched after a quantity and may be a single character. -->
<resources xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools" tools:ignore="InconsistentArrays">
